WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.500
You have reviewed any number of pieces of
tech over all the years.

00:07.500 --> 00:08.000
Yeah.

00:08.000 --> 00:12.500
What would you say was your favorite piece
of tech that you might still be using today?

00:12.500 --> 00:17.000
Oh, that's a good question.

00:17.000 --> 00:22.500
Working for Austin, I have access to a lot
of tech that comes in and out.

00:22.500 --> 00:27.750
And I'm the most indecisive person on the
planet and I have swapped out every little

00:27.750 --> 00:29.000
thing that I've had.

00:29.000 --> 00:36.420
Old school tech is probably my Leatherman
because that thing works for me on every single day.

00:36.740 --> 00:38.380
Like there's not a day that I don't have
it in my pocket.

00:38.860 --> 00:40.100
I don't know, I like my phone a lot.

00:40.320 --> 00:41.500
I just like having it on me.

00:41.640 --> 00:42.440
What kind of phone do you have?

00:42.540 --> 00:45.140
I just got that new iPhone X from work.

00:45.240 --> 00:46.240
Did not know I was getting one.

00:46.420 --> 00:50.570
I was ignoring all the videos because I
was like super salty about like the fact

00:50.570 --> 00:52.800
that my plan didn't end until like
January.

00:53.340 --> 00:55.180
And then Austin was like, yeah, what color
do you want?

00:55.200 --> 00:56.100
I was like, oh sh**.

00:56.100 --> 00:59.660
Something that I've been getting into more
recently and something that I won't ever give up

01:00.540 --> 01:03.380
Are my favorite pair of headphones. Yeah,
I have

01:03.900 --> 01:10.124
the Massdrop AKG K7XX it is probably my
favorite thing, you know, it's it's just

01:10.124 --> 01:11.680
it's nice to go home

01:12.380 --> 01:16.296
Sit down on the couch and just put them on
and listen to music. I'm actually a big

01:16.296 --> 01:17.060
fan of my Pebble

01:17.060 --> 01:19.700
I'm on Android. I'm a PC guy and I have a
Pebble

01:20.220 --> 01:23.660
So I'm like you like are you like the
weird black sheep of this little family?

01:23.660 --> 01:25.720
Yeah, that's why I'm kept as the part-time
guy

01:26.100 --> 01:28.500
Originally, I was an old school watch
person,

01:29.020 --> 01:31.460
and I really didn't want to hold my
features.

01:31.600 --> 01:34.085
I just want something that just pings me
on the wrist whenever I'm getting a

01:34.085 --> 01:35.000
notification, and that's it.

01:35.140 --> 01:36.940
I don't need any of the fitness tracking
thing.

01:37.140 --> 01:39.160
I don't need a watch to tell me that I
should be sleeping more.

01:39.320 --> 01:40.060
I already know that.

01:40.540 --> 01:45.060
Yeah, I'm holding onto the sinking ship as
much as I possibly can.

01:45.140 --> 01:46.740
Well, somebody's got to rearrange the deck
chairs.

01:46.940 --> 01:48.940
It's actually probably a little bit of a
weird answer,

01:49.100 --> 01:50.480
but it's actually the original Apple
Watch.

01:50.480 --> 01:53.960
The Apple Watch fundamentally changed the
way that I sort of lived my life.

01:54.100 --> 01:55.680
I was constantly pulling my phone out.

01:55.680 --> 01:58.990
It was just such a distraction for me and
being able to just put that on the watch

01:58.990 --> 02:00.120
and kind of take a step back

02:00.120 --> 02:03.900
It makes it so easy to triage like oh,
this is an important message from Ken

02:03.900 --> 02:07.680
I need to go find out what that is versus
oh, it's just the 85th email of the day

02:07.680 --> 02:11.280
I don't care. This is all sounds super
dumb like I'm sure no one can relate

02:11.280 --> 02:14.654
But it just to me it really does make a
big difference. That was the longest I've

02:14.654 --> 02:16.320
actually used a single piece of tech and

02:17.160 --> 02:18.660
Probably since I started the channel

02:18.660 --> 02:21.920
I used that first one for two and a half
years had zero problems with that of any kind

02:21.920 --> 02:25.288
It's like it's pretty rare for me to
actually use a piece of tech after the new

02:25.288 --> 02:27.420
one comes out and the new one after that
comes out

02:27.420 --> 02:29.320
Like it's just like no it works. This is
what I like
